invariant: INV-11
file: handshake.c
catches: webpki_session_aes
builds: bin/webpki_session_aes
reason: the client takes AES-128-GCM from the ServerHello and keys its
  handshake directions with ChaCha20, the client twin of the server bug
  e591002 fixed. Every parser test passes; the client cannot open the
  EncryptedExtensions of a server that runs the suite it selected.

--- old
    REC_DIR_INIT_SUITE(&t->rd, h->s_hs, h->suite);
    REC_DIR_INIT_SUITE(&t->wr, h->c_hs, h->suite);
--- new
    rec_dir_init(&t->rd, h->s_hs);
    rec_dir_init(&t->wr, h->c_hs);
